THE CHOICE THIS FILE MAKES, AND HOW TO CHANGE IT
------------------------------------------------
A public repository with no licence file is "all rights reserved" by default, which is what this is -
written down rather than left to be inferred. Nobody may copy, modify, redistribute or host this code
without permission. You may read it, and you may run it for your own use.

It is deliberately the reversible choice. Opening the source later is one commit: replace this file
with the MIT or Apache 2.0 text and say so in the README. Going the other way is not possible, because
a permissive licence cannot be withdrawn from code that has already been published under it. So the
narrow terms come first and the decision stays open.

This does not restrict what the tool computes FOR you. A plan you build in the app is yours, it never
leaves your browser, and the JSON you export is your own data in an open format.

NOT FINANCIAL ADVICE
--------------------
This software is provided for education and illustration. It models UK pensions, ISAs, general
investment accounts, cash, income tax, National Insurance, capital gains tax and pension allowances,
but it is not regulated financial advice and no part of it is a recommendation to buy, sell, hold or
contribute to anything. Its assumptions are visible in the Documentation tab and are assumptions, not
forecasts. Decisions about your own retirement are yours, and worth taking to a regulated adviser.

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT
LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN
